# One line ending everywhere. Without this, `core.autocrlf=true` (the Windows
# default) gives a Windows checkout CRLF for every shipped .md/.yaml/.eta file
# while Linux and macOS see LF, so content-sensitive code and tests behave
# differently per platform (R1 defect 3).
* text=auto eol=lf

# A batch file is the exception: cmd.exe parses `.cmd`/`.bat` line by line and
# an LF-only batch file is unreliable on Windows, which is the one platform
# that runs it. `bin/ambicode.cmd` is already CRLF in the index; keep it so.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
